---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Resources & Field Notes
description: IEEE Software writing, essential software engineering papers, and practical resources curated by Karthik Vaidhyanathan.
permalink: /resources/
---
{% include "partials/related-work-nav.njk" %}
<header class="page-hero page-hero-compact shell">
  <p class="eyebrow">Writing · Reading · Practice</p>
  <h1>Resources & Field Notes</h1>
  <p class="lede">A curated shelf of my IEEE Software writing and research that has shaped how I think about software architecture, intelligent systems, and sustainability.</p>
</header>

<section class="section shell section-rule" id="ieee-software-writing" aria-labelledby="writing-heading">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Software Engineering Radio</p>
      <h2 id="writing-heading">Writing for IEEE Software</h2>
    </div>
    <p>As a member of the Software Engineering Radio team, I write IEEE Software articles that synthesize conversations from multiple episodes into practical engineering themes.</p>
  </div>
  <ol class="media-list">
    {% for item in resources.writing %}
      <li>
        <article>
          <p class="media-meta">SE Radio digest · IEEE Software</p>
          <h3><a href="{{ item.url }}">{{ item.title }}</a></h3>
          <p>{{ item.summary }}</p>
          <p class="project-collaboration">K. Vaidhyanathan. {{ item.publication }}. DOI: {{ item.doi }}.</p>
          <p class="project-collaboration">Topics: {{ item.keywords | join(", ") }}</p>
        </article>
        <p class="media-source">{{ item.year }}</p>
      </li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ol>
</section>

<section class="section shell section-rule" id="essential-reading" aria-labelledby="reading-heading">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">The ideas underneath the work</p>
      <h2 id="reading-heading">Essential reading</h2>
    </div>
    <p>Not a comprehensive bibliography—just papers worth returning to, with a short note on why each one matters.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="project-grid">
    {% for item in resources.reading %}
      <article class="project-card">
        <p class="project-role">{{ item.theme }} · {{ item.year }}</p>
        <h3><a href="{{ item.url }}">{{ item.title }}</a></h3>
        <p class="project-collaboration">{{ item.authors }}</p>
        <p>{{ item.note }}</p>
        <p class="project-collaboration">{{ item.publication }}{% if item.doi %}. DOI: {{ item.doi }}{% endif %}.</p>
      </article>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</section>

<section class="closing shell">
  <p class="eyebrow">A growing collection</p>
  <h2>Useful, annotated, and intentionally selective.</h2>
  <p>I will continue adding research papers, engineering tools, datasets, and practical references. The aim is to explain why something is useful—not to create another unfiltered link directory.</p>
</section>
